      "id": "meet-tomorrow",
      "pattern": "نَتَقَابَلُ + غَدًا",
      "exampleArabic": "نتقابل غدا",
      "exampleTransliteration": "nataqābalu ghadan",
      "exampleEnglish": "We meet each other tomorrow.",
      "grammarNote": "تَقَابَلَ ('to meet each other') is Form VI (تَفَاعَلَ) — reciprocal, built the same way Form V's تَعَلَّمَ (level 62) was built from Form II: a تَـ prefix on Form III قَابَلَ ('to face/meet someone', not taught on its own). Because 'meeting each other' inherently needs two or more people, this verb is naturally used with plural subjects — نَحْنُ, أَنْتُمْ, هُمْ — rather than a single أَنَا or هُوَ, so only those three forms are taught, reusing the plural pronouns and the ـُونَ ending from level 51. Seven of the ten verb forms are now covered outside the base Form I: II, III, IV, V, VI, VIII, and X (يستطيع, level 48).",
      "audio": { "id": "phrase_nataqabalu_ghadan", "text": "نتقابل غدا" },
      "introducedInLevel": 71
    }
  ],
